WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:10.710 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Tucker: IN 2001 LARRY

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.678 line:78%
SINGER COFOUNDED WIKIPEDIA.

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:14.781 line:78%
HE LEFT THE COMPANY SOME YEARS

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:16.549 line:78%
AGO BUT IN THE YEARS SINCE

00:00:14.881 --> 00:00:17.283 line:78%
WIKIPEDIA HAS GONE ON TO BECOME

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:21.054 line:78%
THE WORLD'S SINGLE MOST

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:22.288 line:78%
IMPORTANT SOURCE OF HISTORY, OF

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:24.024 line:78%
INFORMATION AROUND THE WORLD.

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:26.226 line:78%
AND SO IT'S A PROBLEM, WE'VE GOT

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:28.228 line:78%
TO PAY ATTENTION TO AND HE SAID

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:29.095 line:78%
HIMSELF THAT WIKIPEDIA IS NO

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:31.731 line:78%
LONGER A RELIABLE SOURCE OF

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:34.067 line:78%
HONEST INFORMATION.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:35.902 line:78%
HE SAYS THE EDITORS OF WIKIPEDIA

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:37.103 line:78%
USE HIGHLY POLITICIZED SOURCES

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.804 line:78%
AND BLOCK DISSENTING NEWS

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:40.206 line:78%
OUTLETS FROM CONTRIBUTING AT

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:44.110 line:78%
ONCE AGAIN, THAT'S A PROBLEM FOR

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:44.878 line:78%
ALL OF US.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.513 line:78%
LARRY SINGER JOINS US.

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:47.380 line:78%
THANK YOU SO MUCH FOR COMING ON.

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:50.784 line:78%
THIS IS ONE OF THOSE THINGS THAT

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:52.085 line:78%
A LOT OF PEOPLE, A LOT OF US WHO

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.720 line:78%
USE WIKIPEDIA HAVE NOTICED.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:54.821 line:78%
WAIT A MINUTE, I KNOW SOME FACTS

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.423 line:78%
THAT ARE SOMEHOW NOT IN THIS

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:57.390 line:78%
ENTRY OR THEY ARE PLAYING UP

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:59.559 line:78%
SOMETHING THAT DOESN'T SEEM TO

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:00.093 line:78%
BE TRUE OR THIS IS HIGHLY

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.062 line:78%
POLITICIZED.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:04.364 line:78%
YOU SEE THE BIGGER PICTURE HERE,

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:04.931 line:78%
WHAT YOU THINK IS GOING ON?

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:08.701 line:78%
&gt;&gt; IT'S COMPLICATED.

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:11.805 line:78%
FOR ONE THING, WIKIPEDIA ALLOWS

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:17.710 line:78%
ANONYMOUS CONTRIBUTION.

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:18.445 line:78%
AND THAT MEANS THAT BECAUSE IT'S

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:22.148 line:78%
ONE OF THE MOST POPULAR SOURCES

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:27.287 line:78%
OF INFORMATION ONLINE, THERE IS

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:29.222 line:78%
A NATURAL INCENTIVE FOR

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:32.425 line:78%
GOVERNMENTS AND CORPORATIONS,

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:34.894 line:78%
CRIMINAL OPERATIONS TO BASICALLY

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:35.195 line:78%
LEARN HOW TO PLAY THE WIKIPEDIA

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:38.198 line:78%
GAME.

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:38.631 line:78%
SO IT'S OPAQUE TO ME HOW IT

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:43.703 line:78%
REALLY WORKS.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:44.471 line:78%
AND WHAT RESULTS IS BASICALLY

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:49.542 line:78%
ESTABLISHMENT VIEWS ARE THE ONES

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:51.778 line:78%
THAT YOU FIND PUSHED, AND THEY

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:54.948 line:78%
HAVE COMPLETELY ABANDONED THE

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:56.683 line:78%
NEUTRAL POINT OF VIEW.

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:58.852 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Tucker: THAT'S A PROBLEM

00:01:56.783 --> 00:02:00.086 line:78%
BECAUSE IN MY VIEW, WIKIPEDIA

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.287 line:78%
SHAPED THIS COUNTRY'S

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.489 line:78%
UNDERSTANDING OF THE WORLD.

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:04.357 line:78%
IT IS THE PRIMARY SOURCE OF

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:06.326 line:78%
INFORMATION FOR A LOT OF PEOPLE,

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.793 line:78%
MOST PEOPLE ACTUALLY, ABOUT

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:07.727 line:78%
HISTORY.

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:10.563 line:78%
SO WE NEED TO FIX THIS.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:12.365 line:78%
HOW DO YOU THINK WE WOULD DO

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:14.567 line:78%
THAT?

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:18.738 line:78%
&gt;&gt; WELL, THANKS FOR ASKING THAT.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:20.907 line:78%
I DON'T KNOW THAT THERE IS A WAY

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:24.611 line:78%
TO FIX WIKIPEDIA WITHIN

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:25.211 line:78%
WIKIPEDIA.

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:28.481 line:78%
IT'S AN INSTITUTIONALLY

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:30.850 line:78%
CONSERVATIVE PLACE.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:34.854 line:78%
WHAT I WANT TO SEE, ACTUALLY, IS

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:36.723 line:78%
A NEW, BASICALLY KNOWLEDGE

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:38.925 line:78%
COMMENTS, A NETWORK OF ALL THE

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:41.628 line:78%
WIKIPEDIA ARTICLES IN THE WORLD

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:42.662 line:78%
COLLECTED TOGETHER AND MADE IT

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:44.864 line:78%
EASILY SEARCHABLE.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:46.299 line:78%
YOU UNDERSTAND HOW THE

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:53.506 line:78%
BLOGOSPHERE WORKS?

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:54.274 line:78%
THERE IS A STANDARD TO COLLECT

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:56.242 line:78%
BLOGS AND BLOG ARTICLES FROM ALL

00:02:54.374 --> 00:03:00.980 line:78%
OVER THE PLACE.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:03:01.714 line:78%
I WANT THE SAME THING TO HAPPEN

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:04.050 line:78%
BUT WITH ENCYCLOPEDIA ARTICLES

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:06.252 line:78%
AND IF WE DID THAT THEN WE WOULD

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:09.522 line:78%
NO LONGER HAVE TO DEPEND ON

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:11.257 line:78%
WIKIPEDIA AND WE WOULD HAVE,

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:14.527 line:78%
ESPECIALLY IF WE COUPLED THAT

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:16.963 line:78%
WITH A RATING SYSTEM, THEN WE

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:18.364 line:78%
WOULD BE ABLE TO -- MULTIPLE

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:20.066 line:78%
RATING SYSTEMS, ACTUALLY, THAT

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:24.304 line:78%
WOULD ENABLE US TO FIND THE BEST

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:26.072 line:78%
ARTICLES FROM OUR OWN POINT OF

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:27.473 line:78%
VIEW ON EVERY SUBJECT.

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:30.877 line:78%
AND AGAIN, WE WOULD THEN BE FREE

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:32.145 line:78%
OF WIKIPEDIA.

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:34.347 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Tucker: IT MUST KILL YOU AS

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:36.149 line:78%
ONE OF THE PEOPLE WHO HAVE FOUND

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:37.951 line:78%
IT WIKIPEDIA WHICH IS BECOME THE

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:41.421 line:78%
CENTRAL PART OF OUR CULTURE AND

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:44.691 line:78%
INTELLECTUAL LIFE, WEIRD AS IT

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:48.061 line:78%
IS TO SAY, TO --

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:48.461 line:78%
&gt;&gt; I'M SORRY, HOW DO I FEEL

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:49.062 line:78%
ABOUT WHAT?

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:52.131 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Tucker: YOUR ROLE IN

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:53.099 line:78%
CREATING THIS THING THAT NOW

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.499 line:78%
LEADS THE COUNTRY.

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:55.602 line:78%
&gt;&gt; [LAUGHS]

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:56.536 line:78%
I'M EMBARRASSED, TO BE QUITE

00:03:55.735 --> 00:04:00.707 line:78%
HONEST AND I'VE SAID SO FOR A

00:03:56.636 --> 00:04:02.875 line:78%
LONG TIME.

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:06.946 line:78%
I'VE BEEN A LEADING CRITIC OF

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:08.047 line:78%
WIKIPEDIA FOR OVER A DECADE NOW,

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:11.584 line:78%
AND I'VE BEEN TRYING VARIOUS

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:12.652 line:78%
THINGS TO TRY TO IMPROVE ON IT

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:18.258 line:78%
AND I'M SORRY TO ALL THE PEOPLE

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:19.692 line:78%
WHOSE REPUTATIONS HAVE BEEN

00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:25.265 line:78%
SULLIED BY WHAT I GOT STARTED 20

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:27.467 line:78%
YEARS AGO.

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:28.735 line:78%
&gt;&gt; Tucker: GOOGLE HAS HELPED A

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.402 line:78%
LOT BY PROMOTING WIKIPEDIA,

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:29.469 line:78%
WHICH IT DOES.

